WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.866
Coding Exercise 5 is the most important cardinality
exercise in the assignment

00:00:06.611 --> 00:00:11.061
The required grain is one row per patient You need
three counts

00:00:11.284 --> 00:00:16.876
admissions lab tests and prescriptions Patients with
no activity must still

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:22.130
remain Do not directly join all three detail tables
and then use

00:00:22.143 --> 00:00:29.264
COUNT star That creates row combinations and can
inflate the measures Instead

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:33.712
summarize each child table by patient ID inside the
common table expressions

00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:40.043
Each summary should return one row per patient with
one count Then

00:00:40.069 --> 00:00:44.967
LEFT JOIN those summaries to patients Use a
missing-value fallback so a

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:50.404
patient with no activity shows zero instead of NULL
Run and Check

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:53.970
then verify that the number of rows equals the
number of patients

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:58.735
Also inspect a patient with multiple activities and
the patient with no

00:00:58.748 --> 00:00:59.393
activity
